pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iac990274c892d2c6797ba7be36e57269b1d49756" commit="ad61bc6b072264f237add6aecd19887dc629e2ab" commit_message="FAFT: Adding check in dev_boot_usb_checker to verify kernkey_vfy  dev_boot_usb_checker function checks the current boot is from USB in developer mode (Ctrl-U trigger). It confirms the USB boot by checking mainfw_type and by calling is_removable_device_boot function.  It would be better to verify the type of verification done on kernel key (kernkey_vfy) either kernel key is verified using signature or just hash, to confirm the USB boot in developer mode (Ctrl-U trigger).  kernkey_vfy value should be hash in Ctrl-U triggered USB boot in developer mode (it verifies using the hash of the kernel keyblock) and for internal/recovery boot it should be sig (it verifies the good kernel keyblock using the kernel subkey from the firmware).  BUG=None Branch=None TEST= Verified the complete faft_bios &amp; faft_ec suite tests on Soraka (detachable device), all tests are passing. And verified these particular tests on Reef (legacy Ctrl-U device), all tests are passing.  Change-Id: Iac990274c892d2c6797ba7be36e57269b1d49756 Signed-off-by: Lenine Ajagappane &lt;leninex.ajagappane@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/911148 Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="911148" owner_email="leninex.ajagappane@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/48/911148/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="10405.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>